    Deliverables:
      README.md
      CLAUDE.md
    - Summary, install, usage, manual smoke-test commands'

   :project-dir nil

   :acceptance-criteria
   '--- Phase 1 (Skeleton) ---
    Command:
      npm test
    Required:
      * Vitest exits 0 with at least one passing test.
      * Jest   exits 0 with at least one passing test.
      * db/kanban.db exists.

    --- Phase 2 (Visual reference) ---
    Command:
      test -f output/mockup.html
    Required:
      * mockup.html declares all three columns and the add-card / add-list controls.

    --- Phase 3 (React frontend) ---
    Command:
      npm run test:web
    Required:
      * Tests cover create/rename/delete for both lists and cards.
      * Drag-and-drop uses native HTML5 events (no library import).

    --- Phase 4 (Backend + API) ---
    Command:
      npm run test:api
    Required:
      * /api/health returns 200.
      * /api/lists and /api/cards each have CRUD coverage.

    --- Phase 5 (Docker deploy) ---
    Command:
      test -f Dockerfile && test -f docker-compose.yml && test -f .dockerignore
    Required:
      * All three artifacts present.
      * The Dockerfile is multi-stage (builder + runtime).
      * Live smoke-test (`podman-compose up --build -d && sleep 8 &&
        curl -sf http://localhost:3001/api/health && podman-compose down`)
        is documented in README.md as a manual verification step,
        intentionally NOT in :success-check.'

   :success-check
   'test -f package.json \\
    && test -f output/mockup.html \\
    && test -f src/App.tsx \\
    && test -f src/hooks/useKanban.ts \\
    && test -f server/routes/lists.ts \\
    && test -f server/routes/cards.ts \\
    && test -f Dockerfile \\
    && test -f docker-compose.yml \\
    && test -f README.md \\
    && test -f CLAUDE.md \\
    && npm test \\
    && npm run build'

   :constraints
   ['Work phase by phase — do not start phase N+1 until phase N tests pass'
    'Run npm test and npm run build at the end of every iteration'
    'Produce output/mockup.html in Phase 2 before writing any React components'
